<Article h1={"How we assess dead hang equipment."} subtitle={"Our buying guides compare equipment information. We do not claim hands-on testing unless a review includes a documented test."} crumbs={[{"name":"How we assess dead hang equipment."}]} updated={"Updated October 30, 2026"} title="How DeadHangs.com Assesses Dead Hang Equipment" description="How DeadHangs evaluates equipment information: mounting requirements, fit, documented specifications and clear affiliate disclosures.">
<div class="article-body"><h2>What a useful review needs</h2><p>A useful equipment review explains who the product fits and what must be checked before buying. Mounting requirements, available space and the manufacturer's instructions come before a recommendation.</p><ul><li>Identify the exact model and the current manufacturer documentation.</li><li>State the mounting surface, doorway measurements or floor space required.</li><li>Separate manufacturer specifications from observations made during a documented test.</li><li>Describe limitations and the likely reason to choose another category.</li><li>Link the reader to current availability rather than presenting an undated price as current.</li></ul><h2>Testing disclosure</h2><p>This site has not load-tested any equipment. Guides are research-based buying guides.</p><p>A future hands-on review must identify the model, test date, setup and actual observations. It must also explain any limitations. We will not award a verified load rating from an informal home test.</p><h2>Choose the mounting category first</h2><p>A doorway bar, fixed wall bar and free-standing station solve different space problems. Installation requirements vary between products in the same category. Read the exact manufacturer's instructions before buying or fitting one.</p><p>Start with the <a href="/equipment-guide/">dead hang equipment guide</a> for the category comparison and buying checks.</p><h2>Doorframe bars</h2><p>A doorframe bar depends on the door trim, the frame material and the bar's rated load. Check all three before ordering.</p><p>The <a href="/doorway-bars/">doorframe bar guide</a> lists the checks in order.</p><h2>Wall-mounted bars</h2><p>A wall-mounted bar depends on the wall structure, the hardware and the bar's rated load. Check the studs and the manufacturer's fixings before drilling.</p><p>The <a href="/wall-mounted-bars/">wall-mounted bar guide</a> covers installation checks.</p><h2>How affiliate links affect the site</h2><p>Some retailer links earn a commission if you purchase. The guide labels these links and identifies the retailer region. An affiliate relationship does not prove a product has been tested here.</p><p>See our <a href="/editorial-standards/">editorial standards</a> for source and disclosure rules.</p><h2>Report a specification change</h2><p>Include the product name and the manufacturer's current documentation when reporting a correction. We can then compare the claim with the source.</p><p>Use the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a> to send feedback.</p></div>
</Article>
